# bashbasicsbyvk_deps.list - THE central registry of external dependencies (data, never sourced).
#
# ONE place that says: which outside tools / packages the app can need, how to detect each, how to install each on each package
# manager, and which menu / command / tool needs which of them.  The engine is bashbasicsbyvk_deps.sh (bash) with the thin
# python wrapper bashbasicsbyvk_deps.py.  AGENTS.md rule 12: every NEW external dependency is added HERE and asked for through the engine
# (`_dep_need <id|feature>...`, `bashbasicsbyvk_deps.sh <id|feature>...`, `deps.ensure(...)`), never with a private `command -v`/`pip install`/"please install X".
# Build-time toolchains (C compiler, make, Go) are NOT listed: those binaries are compiled before distribution.
#
# Line types ('|' separates fields, '#' starts a comment, a blank line is ignored):
#
#   D|id|kind|probe|packages|label|purpose|needs|flags|note
#       id        lower-case name other code uses ("7z", "numpy").  A feature may not reuse a dependency id.
#       kind      cmd    a program on PATH                      probe = command names, comma separated; ONE of them is enough (7zz,7z,7za,7zr)
#                 pymod  a Python module (system package)       probe = module name
#                 pip    a Python package installed with pip    probe = module[:distribution:minimum.version]
#                 npm    a global npm package                   probe = the command it provides
#                 file   a data file installed by a package     probe = paths, comma separated, ONE existing is enough ($PREFIX is expanded)
#       packages  `manager=name;manager=name`, manager = termux apt dnf yum pacman apk zypper brew (system) | pip | npm | * (any system manager).
#                 `a,b` = alternatives: the first one the manager knows is used (7zip,p7zip-full).
#                 `sys:name` (value for a pip dep) = install it with the SYSTEM manager on that platform instead of pip (Termux: python-numpy).
#                 `@recipe` or `@recipe+dep+dep` = a multi-step install the engine knows (needs those deps first).
#                 A manager that is missing from the list = "not installable here": the dependency is skipped on that platform (termux-api on Linux).
#       label     what the person sees          purpose   one line: what it is needed for (shown in the Installer menu)
#       needs     other dependency ids that must be installed first, space separated
#       flags     auto = the background daemon may install it silently (user-space pip only, retried at most once a day)
#       note      extra line shown in the menu (e.g. an Android app that cannot be installed from the shell)
#
#   G|prefix|pip-name-prefix|version-suffix|needs|label|purpose
#       a family of pip packages: id `tree_sitter_python` -> pip `tree-sitter-python>=0.23`, module `tree_sitter_python`.
#
#   F|feature|title|required|optional
#       a menu / command / tool and what it needs.  `required` and `optional` are dependency ids, space separated;
#       `a/b` = either one is enough (the first is what gets installed).  `optional` ones are only asked for when the caller passes -o.
#       A feature id contains a dot or is not a dependency id.
#
# Order matters only inside the file for readability.

# ── system programs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
D|python3|cmd|python3|termux=python;apt=python3;dnf=python3;yum=python3;pacman=python;apk=python3;zypper=python3;brew=python|Python 3|runs the menus, the file viewport, search, the file index and most tools|||
D|pip|pymod|pip|termux=python-pip;apt=python3-pip;dnf=python3-pip;yum=python3-pip;pacman=python-pip;apk=py3-pip;zypper=python3-pip;brew=python|pip|installs the Python libraries listed below|python3||
D|nodejs|cmd|node|termux=nodejs;apt=nodejs;dnf=nodejs;yum=nodejs;pacman=nodejs;apk=nodejs;zypper=nodejs;brew=node|Node.js|file transfer keys, encryption helpers and the code scanner|||
D|curl|cmd|curl|*=curl|curl|talks to the web (sign-in, uploads, updates, telemetry)|||
D|git|cmd|git|*=git|git|reads and writes repositories (GitHub screens, upgrade, push)|||
D|gh|cmd|gh|termux=gh;apt=@gh-apt+curl;dnf=@gh-dnf;yum=@gh-dnf;pacman=github-cli;apk=github-cli;zypper=gh;brew=gh|GitHub CLI (gh)|signs in to GitHub and creates / pushes repositories|git||
D|rclone|cmd|rclone|*=rclone|rclone|talks to Google Drive and other clouds|||
D|sqlite3|cmd|sqlite3|termux=sqlite;apt=sqlite3;dnf=sqlite;yum=sqlite;pacman=sqlite;apk=sqlite;zypper=sqlite3;brew=sqlite|SQLite|reads the browser / app databases for the load-time report|||
D|tzdata|file|$TZDIR/Asia/Kolkata,/usr/share/zoneinfo/Asia/Kolkata,/usr/lib/zoneinfo/Asia/Kolkata,/usr/share/lib/zoneinfo/Asia/Kolkata,/etc/zoneinfo/Asia/Kolkata,$PREFIX/share/zoneinfo/Asia/Kolkata,/system/usr/share/zoneinfo/tzdata|termux=tzdata;apt=tzdata;dnf=tzdata;yum=tzdata;pacman=tzdata;apk=tzdata;zypper=timezone|Timezone database|lists every timezone and converts times correctly, including daylight saving|||

# ── archive tools ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
D|7z|cmd|7zz,7z,7za,7zr|termux=7zip;apt=7zip,p7zip-full;dnf=p7zip,p7zip-plugins;yum=p7zip;pacman=p7zip;apk=7zip;zypper=7zip,p7zip;brew=sevenzip,p7zip|7-Zip|makes and opens .7z archives (and opens .zip when unzip is missing)|||
D|zip|cmd|zip|*=zip|zip|makes .zip and .skill archives|||
D|unzip|cmd|unzip|*=unzip|unzip|opens .zip and .skill archives|||
D|tar|cmd|tar|*=tar|tar|makes and opens .tar archives (and the compressed tar variants)|||
D|gzip|cmd|gzip|*=gzip|gzip|compresses .tar.gz|||
D|xz|cmd|xz|termux=xz-utils;apt=xz-utils;dnf=xz;yum=xz;pacman=xz;apk=xz;zypper=xz;brew=xz|xz|compresses .tar.xz|||
D|bzip2|cmd|bzip2|*=bzip2|bzip2|compresses .tar.bz2|||
D|zstd|cmd|zstd|*=zstd|zstd|compresses .tar.zst|||
D|lz4|cmd|lz4|*=lz4|lz4|compresses .tar.lz4|||

# ── interpreters for "run this file" (r) that are not part of the base system ──
D|zsh|cmd|zsh|*=zsh|zsh|runs .zsh files|||
D|php|cmd|php|termux=php;apt=php-cli;dnf=php-cli;yum=php-cli;pacman=php;apk=php;zypper=php;brew=php|PHP|runs .php files|||
D|perl|cmd|perl|*=perl|Perl|runs .pl files|||
D|ruby|cmd|ruby|*=ruby|Ruby|runs .rb files|||
D|gcloud|cmd|gcloud||Google Cloud CLI (gcloud)|copies to and from Google Cloud Storage|||Not in the system package lists: install it from https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install

# ── Termux only (not installable elsewhere: skipped on a normal Linux / macOS) ──
D|termux-tools|cmd|termux-open-url|termux=termux-tools|Termux tools (termux-open, termux-open-url, termux-share)|opens links and files and shares them with other Android apps|||
D|termux-api|cmd|termux-clipboard-set|termux=termux-api|Termux:API (clipboard)|reads and writes the Android clipboard|||Also install the Termux:API app (F-Droid / GitHub); the command alone does nothing without it.

# ── npm ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
D|wrangler|npm|wrangler|npm=wrangler|Cloudflare Wrangler CLI|reads a Cloudflare Worker's real configuration (recover)|nodejs||

# ── Python packages (pip) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
D|numpy|pip|numpy|termux=sys:python-numpy;pip=numpy|numpy|number crunching for polyglot and the data tools|pip||
D|pandas|pip|pandas|termux=sys:python-pandas;pip=pandas|pandas|reads and writes spreadsheets / tables for the data tools|pip numpy||
D|openpyxl|pip|openpyxl|pip=openpyxl|openpyxl|reads and writes .xlsx files|pip||
D|rich|pip|rich|pip=rich|rich|coloured console tables and progress bars|pip||
D|esprima|pip|esprima|pip=esprima|esprima|parses JavaScript for the JS audit (otherwise a rougher regex scan is used)|pip||
D|watchdog|pip|watchdog|pip=watchdog|watchdog|watches folders so Recents stays up to date|pip|auto|
D|pyright|pip|pyright|pip=pyright|pyright|type-checks Python for the Python audit|pip||
D|requests|pip|requests|pip=requests|requests|downloads web pages for xtract|pip||
D|bs4|pip|bs4|pip=beautifulsoup4|beautifulsoup4|reads web pages for xtract|pip||
D|tree_sitter|pip|tree_sitter:tree-sitter:0.22|pip=tree-sitter>=0.23|tree-sitter|exact code parsing for polyglot (otherwise the regex parser is used)|pip||
G|tree_sitter_|tree-sitter-|>=0.23|tree_sitter|tree-sitter grammar|exact parsing of one more language for polyglot

# ── menus / commands / tools  ->  what they need  (this IS the dependency map) ──
